A||||5||Lizzy||How hard is it to install new headliner?||||1||
Z||000000||Lizzy||07-06-2001||10:38 AM||||I just my new headliner kit from the Fiero Store.  Any helpful hints on installing it to make the job easier?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ronnie||07-06-2001||10:43 AM||||I just got my headliner recovered this past Tuesday.It was a T-Top, so that made it more difficult, and more flimsy. No problem glueing the material onto the board. The problem comes when trying to re-install the board in the car . You really need an extra set of hands to help hold it in place until you can reattach the sunvisors and coat hooks. After a couple of screwws were installed , then it's a piece of cake.<P>------------------<BR>88GT auto,88Formula T-Top,86GT 4spd<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/3fierossign.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000002||Leadfoot||07-06-2001||12:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ronnie:<BR><B> it's a piece of cake.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>DITTO!  I have a sunroof and the install was easy.  Just carefully remove the fiberglass backing from the car, clean all the old material off it with a stiff brush, spray the glue on, and put the material on.  I pressed down and smoothed the material every five minutes for about and hour.  Looks great!  DON'T spray the glue on the back of the headliner material as it will soak through. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||07-06-2001||12:09 PM||||my first suggestion would be to place the old headliner board on the new fiberglass board and re-mark the areas to be cut out and drilled. I have found, for instance, that the coat hook markings are as much as 2 1/2" off from where they should be. You will also probably have to enlarge the cut-out areas for the third brake light and sunroof latch areas from what they are marked on the new board.<P>Test fit the board in the car prior to covering it with material to make sure all mounting holes are in the properplaces and are the proper sizes!!<P>I have installed several of the fiberglass board headliners and I have had to do remarking and trimming on each one......<P>I hope this helps.....||||reg||1
Z||000004||PAUL88GT||07-06-2001||12:52 PM||||I just replaced the one in my 86se. I found the hardest part was trimming out and installing the molding strip around the sunroof opening.  It is hard to get the right cuts at the corner and leave no exposed material edges. It was my first one (in a Fiero). I was successful, but it took a lot of patience. I also agree it take two people when install the headliner back into the car.  I paid $30 to have an uphostery shop glue the material to the headliner board. This included the headliner cloth.  Paul<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||84Bill||07-06-2001||01:03 PM||||Hi Lizzy Welcome to the Forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>I think there were a few threads on this topic. You can use the search button above and search the Genreal Fiero & the Technical Ares for "Headliner" for example.<BR>I'm sure you will find plenty of great stuff here.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
